# Debugging the TypeScript too: breakpoints in typescript.test.ts stop as well.
# Turn on the setting "IC10 Test: Debug TypeScript" and use the CodeLens, or
# pick the launch configuration "Debug IC10 and TypeScript in the current test
# file" with typescript.test.ts open. Then:
# - Set a breakpoint on "s Heater On 1" here, and one in roomModel in the test.
#   Continue: they take turns, the room's model first each tick, then the chip.
# - The Call Stack shows the IC10 session (its chip) and Vitest's under it.
#   Stop either one and both end.
alias Heater d0
alias Sensor d1
define Low 290
define High 296
loop:
l r0 Sensor Temperature
blt r0 Low heat
bgt r0 High idle
yield
j loop
heat:
s Heater On 1
yield
j loop
idle:
s Heater On 0
yield
j loop
